A 2022 arXiv research paper by 1. On a conjecture concerning the shuffle-compatible permutation statistics

Abstract. The notion of shuffle-compatible permutation statistics was implicit in Stanley’s work on P-partitions and was first
explicitly studied by Gessel and Zhuang. The aim of this paper is to prove that the triple
{\rm(udr,pk,des)}
is shuffle-compatible as conjectured by Gessel and Zhuang, where
{\rm udr}
denotes the number of up-down runs,
{\rm pk}
denotes the peak number, and
{\rm des}
denotes the descent number.
